# Onboarding to {{PROJECT_NAME}}

## 1. Access
- GitHub org `{{ORG}}`: ask the owner for access. Never share credentials in chat or issues.
- Clone every repo side by side (e.g. `~/src/{{ORG}}/`) so agents can read `../{{DOCS_REPO}}`.

## 2. Read (in this order)
1. `README.md` of `{{DOCS_REPO}}`
2. `docs/architecture/service-map.md` — which repo owns what
3. `GLOSSARY.md` — domain vocabulary
4. `docs/adr/` — decisions
5. `docs/agents/how-to-use-agents.md` — agents and skills
6. `docs/agents/ticket-standard.md` — when work is ready

## 3. Work flow
Ticket (`ready-for-agent` / `ready-for-human`) → branch from `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}` → PR with `Closes #n` → CI green → reviews → human merge → staging ({{STAGING_URL}}) → owner releases to production ({{PROD_URL}}).

## 4. Never
- Push to `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`, merge your own unreviewed PR, or run production releases unless you are the owner.
- Paste secrets, tokens or personal data into code, issues, PRs or AI chats.
- Connect to staging/production databases or servers from your laptop or CI without an approved runbook.
- Invent legal/domain facts; mark them "to be validated by {{DOMAIN_EXPERT}}".
